<title>USA: Hilton CEO concerned over ITT asset sales.</title>
<headline>Hilton CEO concerned over ITT asset sales.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilton Hotels Corp Chief Executive Stephen Bollenbach on Wednesday said he was concerned by news that ITT Corp may quickly sell assets to derail Hilton's $6.5 billion bid for the company.</p>
<p>&quot;A fire sale of these assets will bring significantly less value than an orderly sale process,&quot; Bollenbach wrote in a letter to ITT Chairman Rand Araskog.</p>
<p>&quot;Following the combination of our companies, we will be able to work together to review all of ITT's non-core assets and realize the best value for these assets,&quot; Bollenbach wrote.</p>
</text>
